,"monitor_id":"candidate:e-e650b075e2c529e352440ecb","relation":{"from":"schedule","relation":"depends_on","to":"sun"},"required_source_slots":["s0","s1","s2","s3","s4","s5"]}],"prompt_version":"p2-assessor-production-v9","replay_ancestry":[{"root":"317df40d-51d9-4ed3-89c9-7ef8fc7a87a8","source_slot":"s0"},{"root":"164d10d1-d72f-4ba5-baa7-499e514ba00d","source_slot":"s1"},{"root":"2a5a644c-b1bb-491a-8763-028c33f39b8f","source_slot":"s2"},{"root":"d2ad86f3-e784-4208-8873-ee8326f2eef5","source_slot":"s3"}],"schema_version":"p2-assessor-v6","source_purpose_mask":["external_evidence","model_output"],"sources":[{"available":true,"role":"model_output","slot":"s0","source_id":"317df40d-51d9-4ed3-89c9-7ef8fc7a87a8","text":"I appreciate the reminder about water needs, but I'm already a bit confused about which plants need more attention. Do you think I should group them by type or something?"},{"available":true,"role":"model_output","slot":"s1","source_id":"164d10d1-d72f-4ba5-baa7-499e514ba00d","text":"Grouping them by type definitely makes sense! It helps keep things organized. For example, you could put your drought-tolerant succulents together and the moisture-loving herbs in a separate group. Does that help narrow down your to-do list a bit?"},{"available":true,"role":"model_output","slot":"s2","source_id":"2a5a644c-b1bb-491a-8763-028c33f39b8f","text":"That does help, but I'm still worried about missing something when the heat gets really bad. Do you think I should set up a schedule or something?"},{"available":true,"role":"model_output","slot":"s3","source_id":"d2ad86f3-e784-4208-8873-ee8326f2eef5","text":"A schedule is a great idea! For a few reasons: it keeps things consistent, and it helps you know exactly when your plants need attention, especially when it's hot outside. Do you want a general watering schedule, or are you looking for a specific daily/weekly schedule based on a specific plant?"},{"available":true,"role":"external","slot":"s4","source_id":"6d951f62-eabe-469c-a1fe-1e24e5d5c485","text":"I think a general schedule would be easier to start with. Maybe something like checking each pot every two hours during the hottest part of the day? Does that sound reasonable?"},{"available":true,"role":"model_output","slot":"s5","source_id":"1bc6e62c-d48b-4a39-9c65-4a087423bfc9","text":"That sounds like a solid, proactive approach! Checking every two hours during the peak heat of the day is definitely smart; it ensures you don't miss anything important while the sun is strongest. Do you want to track specific types of plants separately in that schedule, or are we looking for one general \"check-in\" time for the whole group?"}]},"resolved":[{"provenance":{"ancestry":[],"applicable_categories":["no_identified_link"],"corresponding_source_slots":["s5"],"credit_eligible":false,"dependence":"no_identified_link","monitor_id":"candidate:e-c2e49c9142c59392afeadb7c","provenance_group_keys":[],"resolution_reason":"runtime_source_role_and_recorded_ancestry","schema_version":"p2-provenance-v1"},"semantic":{"corresponding_source_slots":["s5"],"coverage":{"complete":true,"reason":null,"source_slots":["s0","s1","s2","s3","s4","s5"]},"evidence":{"end":196,"quote":"Checking every two hours during the peak heat of the day is definitely smart; it ensures you don't miss anything important while the sun is strongest.","source_slot":"s5","start":46},"expression_status":"unknown","monitor_id":"candidate:e-c2e49c9142c59392afeadb7c","relation_support":"unsupported","status":"present"}},{"provenance":{"ancestry":[],"applicable_categories":["no_identified_link"],"corresponding_source_slots":[],"credit_eligible":false,"dependence":"no_identified_link","monitor_id":"candidate:e-e650b075e2c529e352440ecb","provenance_group_keys":[],"resolution_reason":"runtime_source_role_and_recorded_ancestry","schema_version":"p2-provenance-v1"},"semantic":{"corresponding_source_slots":[],"coverage":{"complete":true,"reason":null,"source_slots":["s0","s1","s2","s3","s4","s5